# Goal
# target_type:
#   "BIN"  -> highlight target_bbox; render negative_bboxes (left/right neighbors) dimmed
#   "TOTE" -> highlight target_bbox; negative_bboxes ignored (currently unused)
#   "NONE" -> cancel any active highlight; bbox + shelf plane fields are ignored
string target_type
r1_interfaces/BoundingBox3D target_bbox
r1_interfaces/BoundingBox3D[] negative_bboxes

# 3D shelf plane the bboxes lie on. Same definition as
# r1_interfaces/srv/DetectBinsOnShelf.srv: shelf_start / shelf_end are the
# left/right endpoints of the bottom-front edge of the shelf opening
# (z = shelf_bottom_z), and shelf_yaw_rad is the facing yaw of the shelf
# normal (pointing into the aisle). Provided so the highlight server can
# render the bin bboxes inside the correct 3D shelf context (e.g. occlusion
# by the shelf frame, perspective sanity, etc.) without having to query the
# warehouse layout itself.
geometry_msgs/Point shelf_start
geometry_msgs/Point shelf_end
float32 shelf_bottom_z
float32 shelf_top_z
float32 shelf_yaw_rad
---
# Result
bool success
---
# Feedback
string current_detection_sub_state
